+## AWA-897 and the teleconference chronology
+
+The National Archives lists **AWA-897** in Box 98 as a chronology. The seven-page scan begins with the typed title *Chronology of Events, September 11, 2001*. The upper-right handwriting calls it an AAT log of the September 11 operations teleconference and says **“From AAT-1.”** The annotation supplies an office lead. Its writer, date and basis are open. The visible event date supplies no date for the handwriting or the assembly of this copy. [AWA-897, physical p. 1](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913707)
+
+Six distinctive anchors appear on four corresponding pages of **AWA-897** and the held **AWA-610 UAL93** copy. They include the two WTC labels on p. 1, a **1026** UAL93 military position report and the **1041** AA77 qualification on p. 2, the **1526** final timed entry on p. 6, and the p. 7 statement that specific notes are no longer being kept. The separately held six-page **Canoles 212** archive member shares four scoped wording anchors, including the p. 2 rows and the **1526** end entry. The copies contribute a version and source lead. They are dependent evidence for the events described. A common underlying file and direct copying are untested possibilities. [AWA-610 UAL93 copy](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597160) · [Canoles member and prior scope](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5d8fb6fe11486f727b824971ff49af8a4f450cb4/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-item21-receiving-file-counterparts-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Source pins and line locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
